  "findings": [
    "At six writers, command staging averages 12.38-13.44 ms. Preview construction accounts for about 5.05-5.45 ms, capture/collection 3.66-3.97 ms, transaction 2.09-2.29 ms and trim 1.50-1.65 ms. These are approximate nested counters, not an exact per-request attribution.",
    "The private-capture collection path takes 1.30-1.40 ms, including directory listing, reopen/read-back and bounded decoding. Keeping decoding while handing off bounded encoded cuts can remove redundant file I/O.",
    "WAL capture itself averages 2.31-2.51 ms; capture file creation/write/rename takes 1.45-1.56 ms. Disposable capture syncs and image digest/encoding are small in these windows.",
    "No working-image reopen was recorded in timed windows. All timed capture observations were incremental; this profile does not cover checkpoint-generated multi-cut proposals, which require dedicated regression tests.",
    "All four diagnostic windows are error-free with exact replica/archive verification. This is not a control/candidate speedup or sustained-capacity qualification."
  ],
